   "cell_type": "raw",
   "source": [
    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# 🚀 Introduction to Apache Spark with PySpark\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Welcome to the Spark Workshop! This notebook will guide you through the basics of Apache Spark using PySpark.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## What you'll learn:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Creating a SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Creating and manipulating DataFrames\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Basic transformations and actions\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Working with SQL queries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Simple data analysis\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Setting Up Spark\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"First, let's create a SparkSession - the entry point for all Spark functionality.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from pyspark.sql.functions import col, avg, count, sum, desc, when\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spark = SparkSession.builder \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .appName(\\\"Spark Workshop - Intro Lab\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .config(\\\"spark.sql.adaptive.enabled\\\", \\\"true\\\") \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .getOrCreate()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set log level to reduce noise\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spark.sparkContext.setLogLevel(\\\"WARN\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"✅ SparkSession created successfully!\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"📦 Spark version: {spark.version}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"🔧 App name: {spark.sparkContext.appName}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Creating DataFrames\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"DataFrames are the primary data structure in Spark. Let's create some sample data.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Sample employee data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_data = [\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (1, \\\"Alice\\\", \\\"Engineering\\\", 75000, \\\"2020-01-15\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (2, \\\"Bob\\\", \\\"Engineering\\\", 82000, \\\"2019-03-20\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (3, \\\"Charlie\\\", \\\"Sales\\\", 65000, \\\"2021-06-01\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (4, \\\"Diana\\\", \\\"Sales\\\", 72000, \\\"2018-09-10\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (5, \\\"Eve\\\", \\\"Marketing\\\", 68000, \\\"2022-02-28\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (6, \\\"Frank\\\", \\\"Engineering\\\", 90000, \\\"2017-11-05\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (7, \\\"Grace\\\", \\\"Marketing\\\", 71000, \\\"2020-07-22\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (8, \\\"Henry\\\", \\\"Sales\\\", 78000, \\\"2019-12-03\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"columns = [\\\"id\\\", \\\"name\\\", \\\"department\\\", \\\"salary\\\", \\\"hire_date\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Create DataFrame\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df = spark.createDataFrame(employees_data, columns)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📊 Employee DataFrame created!\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Check the schema (column types)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Schema:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.printSchema()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Basic DataFrame Operations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's explore some common DataFrame transformations.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Select specific columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📋 Select name and department:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.select(\\\"name\\\", \\\"department\\\").show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Filter rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"🔍 Engineers with salary > 80000:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.filter(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    (col(\\\"department\\\") == \\\"Engineering\\\") & (col(\\\"salary\\\") > 80000)\\n\",\n",
    "    \").show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Add a new column\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"💰 Adding bonus column (10% of salary):\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_with_bonus = employees_df.withColumn(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"bonus\\\", col(\\\"salary\\\") * 0.10\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_with_bonus.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Sort data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📈 Employees sorted by salary (descending):\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.orderBy(desc(\\\"salary\\\")).show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4. Aggregations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Spark excels at aggregating large datasets. Let's perform some aggregations.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Group by department and calculate statistics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📊 Department Statistics:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"department_stats = employees_df.groupBy(\\\"department\\\").agg(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    count(\\\"*\\\").alias(\\\"employee_count\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    avg(\\\"salary\\\").alias(\\\"avg_salary\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    sum(\\\"salary\\\").alias(\\\"total_salary\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"department_stats.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Overall statistics\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📈 Overall Statistics:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total employees: {employees_df.count()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Average salary: ${employees_df.agg(avg('salary')).collect()[0][0]:,.2f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Total payroll: ${employees_df.agg(sum('salary')).collect()[0][0]:,.2f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5. Using Spark SQL\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Spark allows you to run SQL queries directly on DataFrames.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Register DataFrame as a temporary view\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_df.createOrReplaceTempView(\\\"employees\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Run SQL query\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"🔍 SQL Query - Top earners by department:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result = spark.sql(\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    SELECT \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        department,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        name,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        salary,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY department ORDER BY salary DESC) as rank\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    FROM employees\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"result.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# More complex SQL query\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📊 SQL Query - Department Summary:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spark.sql(\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    SELECT \\n\",\n",
    "    \"        department,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        COUNT(*) as num_employees,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ROUND(AVG(salary), 2) as avg_salary,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        MIN(salary) as min_salary,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        MAX(salary) as max_salary\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    FROM employees\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    GROUP BY department\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ORDER BY avg_salary DESC\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\\"\\\"\\\").show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 6. Working with Conditional Logic\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Let's add some conditional columns to our data.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Add salary tier column\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_with_tier = employees_df.withColumn(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"salary_tier\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    when(col(\\\"salary\\\") >= 85000, \\\"Senior\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .when(col(\\\"salary\\\") >= 70000, \\\"Mid-level\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    .otherwise(\\\"Junior\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"🏷️ Employees with Salary Tier:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_with_tier.select(\\\"name\\\", \\\"department\\\", \\\"salary\\\", \\\"salary_tier\\\").show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Count by tier\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"📊 Employees by Salary Tier:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"employees_with_tier.groupBy(\\\"salary_tier\\\").count().show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 7. Clean Up\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Always remember to stop your SparkSession when done!\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Stop SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"spark.stop()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"✅ SparkSession stopped. Workshop complete!\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 🎉 Congratulations!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"You've completed the Introduction to Spark workshop. You learned how to:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Create and configure a SparkSession\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Create DataFrames from Python data\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Perform basic operations: select, filter, sort\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Add and transform columns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Perform aggregations with groupBy\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Use Spark SQL for complex queries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Apply conditional logic with `when`\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### Next Steps\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Try loading data from CSV/JSON files\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Explore more complex transformations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Learn about Spark's distributed processing capabilities\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Experiment with larger datasets\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
